Then the non-thermal line width ($\delta V_{\rm nt}$) on the core scale around each protostar was computed as $$\begin{equation}
\delta V_{\rm nt} = \sqrt{{\delta V_{\rm ob}}^2 - \frac{kT_{\rm k}}{m_{\rm NH_3}}},
\end{equation}$$

The normalized mass-to-flux ratio ($\lambda$) was also computed for each sample protostar as, $$\begin{equation}
\lambda = 2\pi \sqrt{G}\frac{\Sigma}{B_{\rm pos}}, 
\end{equation}$$
